Insights: Presents practical, security-conscious approaches for deploying AI---particularly offline and open-source LLMs---to improve sustainability, analysis, and digital engineering workflows in defense systems. \textbar\textbar{} TL;DR: This presentation demonstrates how responsibly deployed AI tools can enhance system sustainability, modeling, simulation, and analysis while maintaining data security and human oversight. \textbar\textbar{} Contributions: - Describes baseline AI use cases such as offline LLM assistants for technical documentation and requirements analysis. - Demonstrates AI-assisted database querying, code generation, and simulation-driven analysis. - Emphasizes modular, local, and secure AI architectures suitable for defense environments. - Articulates best practices for responsible AI use, including human-in-the-loop controls and task-level deployment. \textbar\textbar{} Challenges: - Ensuring validity and trustworthiness of AI-generated outputs. - Managing data security and avoiding exposure of classified or proprietary information. - High cost of large-scale AI training and infrastructure. - Need for carefully scoped, measurable AI use cases.
