  note = {Insights: Proposes a framework for applying generative AI to systems engineering under rapid, agile acquisition regimes, emphasizing trustworthy, verifiable, and cognitively augmented AI rather than standalone GenAI tools. \textbar\textbar{} TL;DR: This presentation argues that GenAI can accelerate systems engineering when embedded in cognitive--agentic architectures that combine LLMs with verification, simulation, and optimization tools. \textbar\textbar{} Contributions: - Introduces the concept of Rapid Intelligent Systems Engineering for agile acquisition contexts. - Maps GenAI capabilities to INCOSE systems engineering competencies. - Proposes cognitive--agentic architectures that augment GenAI with trustworthy and verifiable tools. - Identifies high-value GenAI use cases across requirements, architecture, interfaces, and design trade studies. \textbar\textbar{} Challenges: - Standalone GenAI lacks reliability, explainability, and uncertainty awareness. - Trust and verification remain critical barriers to operational adoption. - Defining meaningful metrics for AI-assisted SE performance is nontrivial.
